<title>FINLAND: FINNAIR DEC LOAD FACTOR UP AT 69.8 PCT.</title>
<headline>FINNAIR DEC LOAD FACTOR UP AT 69.8 PCT.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-02-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish national airline Finnair</p>
<p>Oy said in a statement on Friday its passenger load factor rose</p>
<p>3.6 percentage points year-on-year in December to 69.8 percent.</p>
<p>Finnair gave the following statistics:</p>
<p>					Dec 1996    Nov 1996   Yr/yr(pct)</p>
<p> Passengers (thousand)	     474	   504	  +7.3</p>
<p> RPK (million)			 922	   901	  +6.8</p>
<p> RTK (million)			 109	   107	 +10.9</p>
<p> Cargo and mail (thousand kg)  6,481	 5,420	 +18.0</p>
<p> Passenger load factor (pct)    69.8	  66.4	  +3.6 pts</p>
<p>December 1996 totals broken down by flight type:</p>
<p>			Passengers   RPK	 RTK	    Cargo</p>
<p>			thousand   million    million     thousand kg</p>
<p> International	 264	 692	  88	    5,854</p>
<p> Domestic		179	  84	   7		509</p>
<p> Charter		  30	 147	  14		119</p>
<p>Load factor (percent) by flight type:</p>
<p>				  Dec 1996   Nov 1996   Yr/yr (pct pts)</p>
<p> International		  68.8	 62.7	  +2.9</p>
<p> Domestic			 56.7	 54.3	  +3.7</p>
<p>Finnair's financial year runs from April 1 to March 31.</p>
<p>RPK - revenue passenger km (revenue passengers carried</p>
<p>multiplied by km flown)</p>
<p>RTK - revenue tonne km (tonnage of revenue load carried --</p>
<p>passengers, cargo and mail -- multiplied by km flown.</p>
<p>Passenger load factor - RPK as a percentage of available</p>
<p>seat km</p>
<p>Finnair does not give a cargo load factor.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki newsroom +358 - 0 - 680 50 235</p>
</text>
